IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pea-types`
IMPORT `pea-eviction`

-- Protection from Eviction Act 1977 (UK) — GOAL 2: NOTICES TO QUIT (s 5).
--
--   "Is this notice to quit valid, and on what day, at the earliest, can it
--    take effect?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1977-43.txt — s 5. The revised
-- text prints both versions of s 5(1)(b); the version is an input.

§ `Goal 2 — notices to quit`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- s 5(1B) "Nothing in subsection (1) or subsection (1A) above applies to—
-- (a) premises let on an excluded tenancy which is entered into on or after
-- the date on which the Housing Act 1988 came into force unless it is
-- entered into pursuant to a contract made before that date; or (b) premises
-- occupied under an excluded licence." (1C): nor to a Welsh dwelling subject
-- to an occupation contract. (1A): for a licence, only a periodic licence.
@ref s 5(1), (1A)-(1C)
@export Whether s 5 of the Protection from Eviction Act 1977 (UK) applies to a notice to quit: a tenancy of a dwelling, or a periodic licence to occupy a dwelling, that is not an excluded tenancy or licence (s 5(1B)) nor a Welsh occupation contract (s 5(1C)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Occupancy`      @desc The letting and whether it is excluded
      n IS A `Notice to quit`  @desc Whether a licence is periodic, and whether the dwelling is in Wales under an occupation contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5 applies to` o `and` n IF
        o's `let or occupied as a dwelling`
    AND NOT (`is excluded` o)
    AND NOT (n's `a Welsh occupation contract`)
    AND periodicIfLicence
    WHERE
        -- s 8(2) deems a service occupier a tenant only "for the purposes of
        -- Part I"; s 5 is in Part II, so for it they are a licensee, within
        -- s 5 only under a periodic licence (changed after the independent
        -- pass, N38).
        periodicIfLicence MEANS
            CONSIDER o's `kind`
            WHEN `a tenancy` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE n's `a periodic licence`

-- The earliest day the notice can take effect.
--   original s 5(1)(b), and (1A)(b) for a licence: "given not less than 4
--     weeks before the date on which it is to take effect";
--   s 5(1ZA) "(a) where it is given by a tenant in relation to premises let
--     under an assured tenancy, if it is given— (i) not less than any length
--     of time before the date on which the notice is to take effect, not
--     exceeding two months, that the landlord has agreed to in writing, or
--     (ii) in the absence of agreement under sub-paragraph (i), not less than
--     two months before the date on which the notice is to take effect; (b)
--     otherwise, if it is given not less than four weeks before".
--   (1ZB): for a joint assured tenancy the agreement is valid only if made
--     with all the tenants.
@ref s 5(1)(b), (1ZA)-(1ZB), (1A)(b)
@export The earliest day on which a notice to quit (or to end a periodic licence) can take effect under s 5 of the Protection from Eviction Act 1977 (UK): four weeks after it is given; or, as amended by the Renters' Rights Act 2025, for a tenant's notice under an assured tenancy, two months after (the corresponding date) or any shorter period, not exceeding two months, the landlord agreed in writing (with all joint tenants). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Occupancy`      @desc Whether it is a tenancy or a licence
      n IS A `Notice to quit`  @desc The version of s 5, who gives the notice, the day it is given, whether the tenancy is assured, and any period agreed in writing
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day the notice can take effect for` o `and` n MEANS
    IF   amendedAssuredTenantNotice
    THEN CONSIDER n's `period agreed in writing, in days`
         WHEN JUST days THEN
            IF   n's `agreed with all the tenants`
             AND `the day` days `days after` given AT MOST twoMonths
            THEN `the day` days `days after` given
            ELSE twoMonths
         WHEN NOTHING THEN twoMonths
    ELSE `the day` 28 `days after` given
    WHERE
        given MEANS n's `given on`
        twoMonths MEANS `add months` given 2
        isTenancy MEANS
            CONSIDER o's `kind`
            WHEN `a tenancy` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        byTenant MEANS
            CONSIDER n's `given by`
            WHEN `the tenant or licensee` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        amended MEANS
            CONSIDER n's `version`
            WHEN `as amended by the Renters' Rights Act 2025` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        amendedAssuredTenantNotice MEANS amended AND isTenancy AND byTenant AND n's `an assured tenancy`

-- s 5(1) "no notice ... shall be valid unless— (a) it is in writing and
-- contains such information as may be prescribed, and (b)" the period is met.
-- Where s 5 does not apply, it does not invalidate the notice.
@ref s 5(1), (1A)
@export Whether a notice to quit (or to end a periodic licence) meets s 5 of the Protection from Eviction Act 1977 (UK): where s 5 applies, it is in writing with the prescribed information and takes effect no earlier than the earliest day s 5 allows; where s 5 does not apply, s 5 does not invalidate it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Occupancy`      @desc The letting and whether it is excluded
      n IS A `Notice to quit`  @desc The notice: version, who gives it, writing and prescribed information, the day given and the day it is to take effect
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice meets s 5 for` o `and` n IF
        NOT (`s 5 applies to` o `and` n)
    OR  (    n's `in writing with the prescribed information`
         AND n's `to take effect on` AT LEAST `the earliest day the notice can take effect for` o `and` n)
